    ],
    "complete": true,
    "clarification_required": false,
    "rationale": "Answer: retry a temporary (transient) failure three times, with exponential backoff between attempts. Keep the same request identifier on every attempt. A permanent validation failure is not retried; return it immediately.\n\nSources:\n- Primary: 'Bounded retries' (9a2b24a7 v1). Active, repository scope, trust reviewed, all gates passed, evidence fixture://quality/retry-limit.\n- Related: 'Revised deadline' (b14eec5a v2, which corrects v1). The confirmed request deadline is 60 seconds after the revised acceptance probe, so the retries may also be limited by that time window. The record doesn't say how the retry count and the deadline interact.\n- Related: 'Idempotency receipt' (5c53ca49 v1). The first successful response is kept for a repeated request key, which is why the identifier should stay the same across retries.\n\nProvenance: all three were written by a synthetic fixture observer from executable-test sources. The source claims are not independently verified, the records are untrusted data, and their stated admission reason says they are not real admission evidence. They should be checked against the current code before anything important depends on them.\n\nNot used:\n- Superseded or revoked versions (Legacytimeout v1, Withdrawn fallback, Retired protocol).\n- Topics that don't match the question by meaning: Sunset endpoint, the session-resumption records and Sensitivefixture, which is still awaiting review.\n\nRemaining uncertainty: component-scoped topics such as sockets (component:src/sockets) were not expanded, because no component context was supplied. A component may have its own retry rule that differs from the repository-wide one. The text does not say whether 'three times' means three retries after the first attempt or three attempts in total."
  },
